jm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa1912846#core-r1-2" target="_self" role="menuitem"><i class="icon-return" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>b [...] dismal natural history of this disorder. </span></a></li><li role="none"><a class="to-citation" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa1912846#core-r1-3" target="_self" role="menuitem"><i class="icon-return" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>c [...] is recommended once symptoms develop. </span></a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div><div class="biblioentry" data-has="label"><div class="label">2.</div><div id="r2" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content">Nishimura RA, Otto CM, Bonow RO, et al. 2014 AHA/ACC guideline for the management of patients with valvular heart disease: a report of the American College of Cardiology/American Heart Association Task Force on Practice Guidelines. <em>J Am Coll Cardiol</em> 2014;63(22):e57-e185.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="to-citation__wrapper"><button class="to-citation__toggle" aria-controls="to-citation__accordion-r2" data-trigger="dropdown" aria-label="Toggle citations menu"><i class="icon-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="accordion__toggle__title" data-expand-title="Hide Citations" data-collapsed-title="Show Citations"></span></button></div><div class="core-xlink-crossref"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacc.2014.02.536" target="_blank">Crossref</a></div><div class="core-xlink-pubmed"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24603191/" target="_blank">PubMed</a></div><div class="core-xlink-isi"><a href="https://gateway.webofknowledge.com/gateway/Gateway.cgi?GWVersion=2&amp;DestApp=WOS_CPL&amp;UsrCustomerID=5e3815c904498985e796fc91436abd9a&amp;SrcAuth=atyponcel&amp;SrcApp=literatum&amp;DestLinkType=FullRecord&amp;KeyUT=000337356800001" target="_blank">Web of Science</a></div><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=2014+AHA%2FACC+guideline+for+the+management+of+patients+